{
  // audit-ci config — runs npm audit and enforces a "high" threshold.
  // See: https://github.com/IBM/audit-ci
  "high": true,

  // Allowlisted advisories — known upstream issues with no available fix.
  // Each entry must include a comment explaining the rationale and an expected
  // resolution so the allowlist doesn't silently persist forever.
  //
  // Keep this as short as possible: only advisories with genuinely no fixed
  // version published belong here.
  //
  // History: the two multer DoS advisories (GHSA-72gw-mp4g-v24j,
  // GHSA-3p4h-7m6x-2hcm) were allowlisted here on the stated grounds that
  // "@nestjs/platform-express pins multer to exactly 2.1.1" and that "npm
  // overrides cannot bypass exact-version pins". That diagnosis was wrong on both
  // counts. The real cause was an unresolvable dependency tree (eslint 10 vs the
  // eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y / eslint-plugin-react peer ranges), which made npm
  // silently reuse the existing node_modules instead of re-resolving — so no
  // override in this repo ever took effect, and transitive deps never advanced.
  // With the peer conflict fixed and the tree re-resolved, multer lands on 2.2.0
  // via @nestjs/platform-express@11.1.28 and both advisories are gone.
  //
  // Lesson: before allowlisting, verify the fixed version is genuinely
  // unreachable — `npm audit`'s `range` field is a UNION across advisories, so it
  // routinely looks like no fix exists when one does.
  //
  // GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm (braces <=3.0.3 stack-exhaustion DoS, dev-only via
  // @next/eslint-plugin-next > fast-glob > micromatch) was allowlisted here from
  // 2026-09-18 with no patched version available. GitHub withdrew the advisory on
  // 2026-10-23 and audit-ci began printing "Consider not allowlisting", so the
  // entry was removed.
  "allowlist": [],
}
